# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 1: METADATA BLOCK
# ( Identity, Provenance, Scaling Telemetry & Architectural Boundary Contracts )
# ==============================================================================
# @project       OmniCode Framework
# @file          .gitignore
# @id            root.vcs.gitignore
# @layer         Root Version Control Boundary (Track 5 Operations)
# @archetype     vcs_manifest | operational
# @version       0.1.3-dev
# @interface_rev Rev 5
# @date          2026-11-20
# @author        CreativeWorkzStudio LLC / ProfessorSeanEX (Seanje Lenox-Wise)
# @repository    https://github.com/Novaking34/OmniCode_Framework
# @system        OmniCode Multi-Track Framework & Mounted Submodule Ecosystem
# @role          Repository-Wide Exclusion Boundary Between Source and Artifacts
# @maturity      Rev 5 Baseline | v0.1.3 Mass Alignment Wave
# @chassis       deterministic-ignore | Zero binary bloat & zero secret leakage
# @scale         O(1) path filtering across Tracks 0-5 & root submodules
# @seams         in: git index | guards: target/, .env, scrolls, QEMU images
# @invariants    1. Universal 5-Block Lifecycle Protocol (Rev 5).
#                2. Live secrets (`.env`, `.env.local`) are NEVER committed.
#                3. Ephemeral binaries, QEMU ISOs, and REPL histories remain
#                   strictly untracked.
#                4. Canonical `.omni`, `.tape`, `.rs`, `.c`, `.go`, and docs
#                   remain tracked.
#                5. Mounted submodules (`FaithNet/`, `Tenebris-and-Lux/`)
#                   manage their own internal `.gitignore` rules independently.
#
# PURPOSE & ARCHITECTURAL ROLE:
#   Establishes the hard boundary between permanent, version-controlled source
#   assets and ephemeral compiler outputs, bare-metal disk images, episodic
#   runtime caches, and private host secrets.
#
#   ### For Everyday Builders & AI Agents:
#   Protects against accidental `git add .` mistakes—keeping private `.env`
#   secrets, multi-gigabyte OS disk images, and local terminal histories out of
#   public Git history while keeping all real source files clean and visible.
#
#   ### For Systems Programmers & Engine Architects:
#   Partitions ignore patterns cleanly across Rust/LLVM build targets, Track 0
#   bare-metal media outputs, Track 4 runtime scrolls/weights, editor bundles,
#   and OS/IDE noise without interfering with submodule gitlink entries.
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 2: OPENING BLOCK
# ( Compiler Intermediates, Native Build Targets & Object Caches )
# ==============================================================================
# Rust/Cargo build directory (debug, release, cross-target & test binaries)
/target/
target/

# Compiler object files, static archives, and dynamic shared libraries
*.o
*.a
*.rlib
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Cargo incremental build caches and patch backups
*.cargo-ok
*.orig

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 3: BODY BLOCK
# ( Bare-Metal Media, Runtime Memory, Apps, Secrets & Workstation Hygiene )
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3.1 Distribution Packages & Track 0 Bare-Metal Bootable Media
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native distribution tarballs and installers
dist/*.tar.gz
dist/*.zip
!dist/.gitkeep
infra/dist/*.tar.gz
infra/dist/*.zip
!infra/dist/.gitkeep
**/dist/*.tar.gz
**/dist/*.zip
!**/dist/.gitkeep

# Bare-metal kernel bootable ISOs, raw binaries, ELF/EFI & QEMU disk images
*.iso
*.bin
*_bin
*.img
*.qcow2
*.elf
*.efi
*.EFI
NvVars
**/NvVars

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3.2 Track 4 Runtime State, Episodic Memory Scrolls & Model Weights
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inscribed neural-symbolic execution traces and runtime telemetry logs
*.scroll
*.log
!*.omni
!*.tape
storage/scrolls/**
**/storage/scrolls/**
runtime/scrolls/**
**/scrolls/**
!**/scrolls/**/.gitkeep
!**/storage/scrolls/**/.gitkeep

# Neural brain weight checkpoints & plasticity caches
*.weights
storage/weights/
**/storage/weights/

# Root workspace runtime storage mirror (canonical assets live in Track 4)
/storage/

# Track 4: Multi-translation scripture vault (preserved locally on disk)
scripture/
**/scripture/

# Interactive REPL & debugger command histories (local developer keystrokes)
.omnicode_history
.gdb_history

# Process crash core dumps
/core
/core.*
core.[0-9]*
vgcore.*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3.3 Track 3 Apps, Editor Extensions, Node & Python Caches
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaged VS Code extension archives
apps/editors/vscode/*.vsix
editors/vscode/*.vsix
*.vsix

# Node.js dependency trees and npm package caches
node_modules/
.npm/

# Python virtual environments, bytecode caches & cloud CLI state
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
env/
venv/
.oci-cli/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3.4 Private Environment Secrets & Temporary Editor Swap Files
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment variables and tokens (NEVER commit live secrets)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Temporary, swap, and backup editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp
*.bak

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3.5 Host Operating System & Local IDE Metadata
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS Finder / Spotlight metadata
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows Explorer metadata
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local IDE configuration caches (preserve tracked .vscode/settings.json)
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
.vscode/*.log
.vscode/.browse.*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3.6 Temporary Clean-Room Staging Quarantine (1:1 Parity Aperture)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore staged Track 0-7 folders under omnicode/ by default, while opening an
# explicit parity aperture for verified clean-room folders (starting with
# `.agents/`) alongside deprecated top-level `![...]` anchors before committing.
/omnicode/*
!/omnicode/.agents/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: AUDIT PROCEDURES BLOCK
# ( Exclusion Verification & Secret Quarantine Tripwires )
# ==============================================================================
# Pre-flight verification commands:
#   1. Confirm live secrets and build outputs are ignored:
#        git check-ignore -v .env target/ .omnicode_history
#   2. Confirm canonical templates and submodules are NOT ignored:
#        git check-ignore -v .env.example .gitmodules FaithNet Tenebris-and-Lux
#        (must return exit code 1 / empty output)
#   3. Confirm zero accidentally tracked secrets in index:
#        git ls-files .env '*.weights' '*.iso'

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 5: CLOSING BLOCK
# ( Invariant Boundary Guarantees & Workspace Seal )
# ==============================================================================
# INVARIANT BOUNDARY GUARANTEE:
#   - All canonical source reels (`*.omni`), process tapes (`*.tape`), Rust VM
#     crates (`<TRACK 1>`), Track 2 stdlib/lexicon, Track 5 docs, `.agents/`,
#     and mounted submodule gitlinks (`FaithNet`, `Tenebris-and-Lux`) remain
#     strictly tracked, deterministic, and clean.
# Status: GITIGNORE_SEALED (+1:PROCEED)
# ==============================================================================
